==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ey|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|awjō|lang=is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/eiː/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|eiː|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|ei}}, {{l|is|Ey}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|eyjar|eyjar}}

# [[island]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s1||ey|j=j}}
The dative singular ''eyju'' / ''eyjunnar'' also occurs, but is on its own indistinguishable from the dative of the weak form {{term|eyja|lang=is}}.

